 "lean": -5.0, "environment": 8.7, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": 1.95}, "rating_margin": 3.4, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 6.28, "baseline_margin": 6.34, "analyst_adjustment": -0.34, "key_factors": ["Jamie Ager's massive fundraising edge ($5.9M vs $0.4M) and outside groups abandoning Balkcom, including a canceled $1M+ Trump super PAC buy", "Open seat after Chuck Edwards withdrew, removing incumbent advantage in an R+5 district", "Prediction markets price the Democrat at roughly 78-83%, and most expert raters call it a Democratic flip", "Thin polling: one recent Emerson poll shows Ager up 13, but earlier Democratic-sponsored polls were much closer"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point to a Republican-leaning district, but the open seat, Ager's overwhelming financial advantage, the canceled GOP outside spending, and markets pricing the Democrat near 80% all point the same direction. The single recent independent poll and expert consensus support a clear Democratic edge, tempered by the district's partisan lean and limited polling.", "watch": "Any sign that national Republican money returns to the district, or new polling showing Balkcom closing within single digits, would move this back toward a tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Chuck Edwards (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's 11th District is an open seat this year after Republican Chuck Edwards withdrew, leaving Republican Jennifer Balkcom and Democrat Jamie Ager, both from farming families, to compete in a mountain district that leaned Republican by about five points in recent cycles. The national environment favors Democrats, and the seat has emerged as a top flip opportunity.\n\nAger has raised roughly $5.9 million to Balkcom's $400,000, and a Trump-aligned super PAC canceled more than $1 million in planned ads supporting her. One recent Emerson poll showed Ager ahead by double digits, though earlier surveys were tighter. Markets and most expert ratings give the Democrat a clear edge, with a few raters calling it a tossup. The district's Republican lean keeps this from being safe, but the weight of evidence favors Ager.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5972, "margin": 1.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6249, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6236, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6239, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5922, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5614, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6011, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6565, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6466, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.684, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6607, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6845, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6944, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6524, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6027, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.5927, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6347, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6298, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6269, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.6209, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.6546, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.6842, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.7215, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.6511, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.663, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-17", "p_dem": 0.661, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-18", "p_dem": 0.6563, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-19", "p_dem": 0.7097, "margin": 3.8}, {"date": "2026-10-20", "p_dem": 0.6575, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-21", "p_dem": 0.7335, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-22", "p_dem": 0.799, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-23", "p_dem": 0.8504, "margin": 6.0}]}